---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What a pull request passes before it merges
    accDescr: A pull request changes code or a workflow. Each workflow starts only when every action that it runs, and every action that these run in turn, is one of GitHub or matches a pattern of the list in the settings as code; a workflow that names another fails to start. The required checks then pass, and CodeQL and zizmor upload their analyses of the pull request. GitHub compares each with that of main: a new alert of CodeQL of high or critical severity, or a new error, stops the merge, and so does every new alert of zizmor; an alert that main has already doesn't. Otherwise the pull request merges.

    change(["A pull request changes code or a workflow"])
    start["Each workflow starts only when every action<br>that it runs is GitHub's or on the list<br>of the settings as code"]
    blocked["An action that isn't on the list:<br>the workflow fails to start"]
    checks["Every required check passes, and CodeQL<br>and zizmor upload their analyses<br>of the pull request"]
    alert["A new alert of CodeQL of high or critical<br>severity or a new error, any new alert<br>of zizmor: the merge stops; an alert<br>that main has already doesn't"]
    merge(["The pull request merges"])

    change --> start
    start --> checks
    start -. "an unlisted action" .-> blocked
    checks --> merge
    checks -. "a new alert" .-> alert

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class start,checks bot
    class change,blocked,alert person
    class merge done
